      "content": "That's a tough call. If we pull this now, after we've already hinted at it to the press, it's going to look like we're being reckless with our curation. It could hurt our reputation for catching these things before they hit the press. \n\nBut on the other hand, if we publish and it gets debunked in a month, that's even worse for the journal's prestige. Is there any way to frame this as a 'preliminary finding' or perhaps suggest they include a heavy disclaimer about the statistical adjustments in the discussion section? Could we potentially salvage the issue without a full rejection?",
